7:00","id":255762,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>genesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/174324-heirs-to-hell-questions?p=255490#post255490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Can Demons use &quot;Gathering Aether&quot; to gather one point of ambient aether when none of the more usual methods are available (such as access to Infrastructure, stockpiles etc.)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Demons cannot use the Gathering Aether mechanics - their equivalent method of aggregation is to assume demonic form and let God's loose change funnel into the metaphysical couch-cushion that is your old severance package.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T12:45:18-07:00","id":256200,"title":"","content":"<br /> It shouldn't happen often, but I can imagine a very dramatic scene where a Demon mother's cover is completely blown and the shock causes her directly go into labor...giving birth to a demon. <br /> <br /> I'm picturing her in the backseat of a car, speeding along the highway at 100+mph...being chased by hordes of angels, all the while wondering, if either one survives the birth, what the child will be. And if they both do survive, can they retain cover afterwards.<br /> <br /> How can an infant even have a cover? I have heirs, but haven't given it a full read yet, so that question may be already answered.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3854-darthcoffee","name":"darthcoffee","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3854_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"46"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T15:20:01-07:00","id":256290,"title":"","content":"Hey All,<br /> <br /> Beware of the wall of text below. I hope it's as interesting to read as it was to research it!<br /> <br /> I'm pretty glad this thread came up again because looking through the <b>&quot;Demon-Blooded Genetics&quot;</b> side bar I see some inconsistencies with how it works.<br /> <br /> Now I am pretty sure the easy answer to these is &quot;ST fiat&quot; instead of super hard rules but I wanted to put it out there to see if I'm just interpreting this wrong.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heirs to Hell page 17 &quot;Demon-Blooded Genetics[B</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;[/B]]... Demon-Blooded have the recessive Fractal (f) and/or Offspring (o) traits, while mortals with no Demon blood in them have the dominant Human (h) trait.<br /> <br /> Fractals always have the (f,f) combination. The Offspring are Demon-Blooded with the (o,o) or (f,o) combination (the (o) trait only becomes dominant when paired with the Fractal trait). Latents either have the (h,f) or (h,o) combination, and all humans have (h,h)<br /> <br /> Fractals and Offspring born to Demons are always (f,f) or (o,o). After that the Demon-Blooded only pass on only one of those (f)'s or (o)'s so the Fractal passes on the (f) and the Offspring passes on the (o). Because all Mortals who don't have demon blooded pass on the dominant trait (h), the children of Fractals and Offspring are always Latents ((h,f) or (h,o)) unless the other parent is a Demon-Blooded (either a Fractal, Offspring, or Latent).<br /> <br /> Demon/Demon and Demon/Fractal pairs always produce Fractals. Demon/Offspring and Demon/Latent pairs produce Offspring half of the time and Fractals the other half of the time. Demon/Human Pairs ... always produce Offspring.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heirs to Hell page 17 &quot;Special Kinds of Hell&quot;</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">... Although Offspring are most often the result of Demon/Human pairings, they may also be the result of Fractal/Human, Fractal/Offspring, or Offspring/Offspring parents. In rare cases, Offspring are born of two Latent parents ...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> ... Most of the children of Offspring are Latents...<br /> <br /> ... Latents only pass on their Demon-Blood Half of the time ...<br /> <br /> If two Latents have a child together, that child has a small chance of being born Offspring...<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Nearly all Fractals are born from two Demon parents, although some are the child of two Fractals, or a Fractal and a Demon or Offspring. In very rare cases two Offspring with Fractal ancestors will have a Fractal child.</div> </div> </div> </div>So we know the following:<br /> Humans: (h,h)<br /> Latents: (h,f) ; (h,o)<br /> Offspring: (o,o) ; (o,f)<br /> Fractals: (f,f)<br /> Demons: (?,?)<br /> <br /> <b>So the question is:</b><br /> 1. what do Demon's have?<br /> <br /> do they randomly have (o,o) ; (o,f) ; or (f,f) like Fractals and some Offspring?<br /> Or are Demon's Special and have a Tri-Gene system like the following: (o,o,f) ((two (o) traits would make it more likely to pass on an Offspring trait rather than Fractal trait which would be inline with how rare Fractals are.<br /> <br /> Now for a visual example for what a Child would inherit based on the different combinations (for the Purpose of moving on, I am going to assume that Demons have two Offspring traits and one Fractal trait). Please note that I've only included 4 genes tables. I made 27 of them in a separate Excel sheet. <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; width: 371px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Demon (o,o,f)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Demon</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">f</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o,o (offspring)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o,o (offspring)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o,f (offspring)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o,o (offspring)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o,o (offspring)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o,f (offspring)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">f</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o,f (offspring)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o,f (offspring)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">f,f (Fractal)</td> </tr> </table></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; width: 268px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Fractal (f,f)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">f</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">f</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">f</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">f,f (Fractal)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">f,f (Fractal)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">f</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">f,f (Fractal)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">f,f (Fractal)</td> </tr> </table></div> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; width: 268px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Offspring (o,o)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o,o (Offspring)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o,o (Offspring)</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o,o (Offspring)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">o,o (Offspring)</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; width: 268px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Latent (h,o)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" 