 0px; padding: 0px\">h</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Human (h,h)</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">h,f (latent)</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <br /> <br /> And here is the total possibilities and how likely they are:<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode__table--wrapper text_table_\"><table class=\"b-bbcode__table text_table\" style=\"border-spacing: 0px; width: 533px\"><tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Demon/Demon Chances:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">89% OffSpring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">11% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Demon/Fractal Chances:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">67% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">33% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Demon/Offspring Chances:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">91% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">8% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Demon/Latent Chances:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">42% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">8% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">50% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Demon/Human Chances:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">100% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Fractal/Fractal Chances:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">100% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Fractal/Offspring Changes:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">75% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">25% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Fractal/Latent Chances:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">25% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">25% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">50% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Fractal/Human Chances</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">100% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Offspring/Offspring Chances:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">92% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">8% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Offspring/Latent Chances:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">44% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">6% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">50% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Offspring/Human Chances:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">100% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\"></td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Latent/Latent Chances:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">17% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">8% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">50% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">3% Human</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Latent/Human Chances:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">0% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">50% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">50% Human</td> </tr> <tr valign=\"top\" class=\"text_table_tr\"><td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">Total Chances:</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">39% Offspring</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">17% Fractal</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">39% Latent</td> <td class=\"text_table_td\" style=\"border-width: 0px; padding: 0px\">4% Human</td> </tr> </table></div> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fractals and Offspring born to Demons are always (f,f) or (o,o). </div> </div> </div>How can this work? This boils down to what do Demon's have (ei what do they pass on and how is it chosen that they pass on what they do).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demon/Demon and Demon/Fractal pairs always produce Fractals. </div> </div> </div>I'm using a tri-gene system for Demon's because that would make the most sense so by that I found this to be false. From my calculations I found that Demon/Demon pairs bore fractals a mere 11% of the time and Demon/Fractal pairs bore Fractals 33% of the time which is far from <b>always</b> and more in line with how rare they are suppose to be.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demon/Offspring and Demon/Latent pairs produce Offspring half of the time and Fractals the other half of the time. </div> </div> </div>Again not what I got. I got Demon/Offspring pairs producing Offspring 91% of the time and Fractals a mere 8% of the time.<br /> <br /> While my Demon/Latent pairs produced Offspring 42% of the time and Fractals 8% of the time.<br /> <br /> Both these numbers seem to match to the lore but not the table in the sidebar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Demon/Human Pairs ... always produce Offspring. </div> </div> </div>This is just to reiterate the point I'm making but:<br /> <br /> I got Latents 100% of the time with Demon/Human pairs.<br /> <br /> I think this one is the most important one for my point (and how I noticed it).<br /> <br /> If Latents are either (h,f) or (h,o) then there is no possible way that pairs with one Human will result in anything other than either Human or the more likely Latent.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Although Offspring are most often the result of Demon/Human pairings, they may also be the result of Fractal/Human </div> </div> </div>My findings:<br /> Offspring are most often the result of Demon/Offspring pairs.<br /> They can also be the result of every pairing except the following: Demon/Human, Fractal/Fractal, Fractal/Human, Offspring/Human, and Latent/Human.<br /> <br /> The most often result of Demon/Human is Latent (100%)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Most of the children of Offspring are Latents </div> </div> </div>My Findings: Most of the children of Offspring are Offspring (60%).<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> _________________________________________<br /> <br /> tl;dr<br /> I'm seeing some weird things with the numbers. It's likely because I don't know what determines what a Demon's traits. As well as the simple math of any pairing with a Human having to result in a Latent or a Human simply because it <b>has</b> to contribute an (h) gene.<br /> <br /> If anyone can think of something I missed that could have caused my confusion let me know. Otherwise I'll prolly use my Tri-Gene Demon Blood tables for figuring things out (simply because it makes sense to me now and now that I've made it I feel rather proud of the thing I've created <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> )<br /> <br /> <br /> Sorry for the long post <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> -X<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT:</b> It occurs to me now that demons could have the following: ((f,f),(o,o)), which would mean that it would always pass on either (f,f) or (o,o) (which would override whatever the partner has and automatically replace it with pure homogeneous Fractal or Offspring traits.<br /> <br /> This doesn't solve everything but it is an idea for what Demon's give off.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>EDIT 2:</b> I will be rather sad if no one reads this. I put a lot into this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":654,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","user":"xiongrey","date":". 09-13-2014, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T17:31:07-07:00","id":256379,"title":"","content":"I read it. I liked it. Be proud! I will probably use it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3855-gebbethine","name":"gebbethine","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3855_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"233"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-13T22:55:01-07:00","id":256538,"title":"","content":"Heh. I actually wrote up a similar table when I was writing that sidebar, and much of yours matches mine.<br /> <br /> The design goal was to come up with a way for Offspring (and to a lesser extent, Fractals) to exist who didn't have demon parents. Demon-blooded children of demon-blooded were one side of that. The other side was to address the tropes of &quot;I didn't find out I was demon-blooded until a weird cult kidnapped me and tried to sacrifice me to their god&quot; and &quot;Little Johnny is different from the other kids at school, and we have no idea why.&quot; These are conventions of the &quot;demon child&quot; sub-genre, and I didn't want to ignore any of them, so I tried to come up with something reasonably logical to explain why all these different situations were possible. This was my solution.<br /> <br /> As the sidebar says, demon blood isn't a literal gene.That is simply a useful shorthand to explain why most Offspring give birth to Latents, but occasionally two Latents will produce an Offspring (or, rarely, a Fractal) child they are not at all equipped to care for. For Fractals, Offspring, and Latents, demon blood pretty much behaves the same way as recessive genes. As soon as a demon becomes involved, though, Gregory Mendel is going to throw up his hands.<br /> <br /> It's really quite simple:<br /> <br /> - If a demon pairs with a demon or a Fractal the result is always a Fractal (ff). The involvement of the demon &quot;maximizes&quot; the demon blood and leaves the children as close to demonic as the demon-blooded can get.<br /> - If a demon pairs with an Offspring or a Latent (basically, any non-Fractal with demon blood), the result a Fractal (ff) half the time and an Offspring (oo) the other half of the time. The demon's involvement &quot;maximizes&quot; the demon blood half the time (ff) and leaves it on not-quite-the-maximum-setting the other half of the time (oo).<br /> - If a demon pairs with a human with no demon blood, the result is always an Offspring (oo), since there is no demon blood to intensify.<br /> - A pure demon is never the result of any children born of demons or demon-blooded (unless you really want it to be that way in your chronicle, of course).<br /> <br /> Once that demon blood is out &quot;in the wild,&quot; the genetics metaphor works fine most of the time. Demon-blooded parents don't produce Fractals or Offspring unless the other parent is also demon-blooded (including Latents, who might not realize they are demon-blooded), although they do make Latents (100% of the time for Fractals/Offspring and 50% of the time for a Latent parent).<br /> <br /> Latents also have kind of a weird catch. If something &quot;activates&quot; their demon blood, their &quot;demon-blooded genetics&quot; change, adding an o (making them Offspring). Depending on whether their demon blood is f or o, they may end up pure-blooded Offspring (oo) or hybrid Offspring (fo). In neither case do they wind up as Fractals (again, unless your chronicle benefits from such an event). So yes, the child they have before that encounter with the God-Machine only has a 50% chance of being a Latent (assuming the other parent is pure human), while any children born after that nasty shock will always be Latents (and might be Fractals or Offspring, depending on the status of the other parent).<br /> <br /> Does that help make more sense out of this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=\"_blank\">Onyx Path Freelancer</a></b> and former Deviant line developer.<br /> <br /> Deviant projects now on STV: <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/486079/Shallow-Graves?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Shallow Graves</b></a> and <a href=\"https://site.storytellersvault.com/product/550535/Black-Vans?affiliate_id=54122\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Black Vans</b></a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://patreon.com/Dayzdark\" target=\"_blank\">Updates and excerpts of current projects available here</a>.\u200b","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1094-eric-zawadzki","name":"Eric Zawadzki","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T12:51:31-07:00","id":256760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Zawadzki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/174324-heirs-to-hell-questions?p=256538#post256538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Does that help make more sense out of this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually that clears up all the confusion I had! I was thinking about it too literally in the with the genes tables. <br /> <br /> It makes sense now that demons &quot;activate&quot; or &quot;upgrade&quot; the demon blood within a child. It also makes sense because it's consistent with the fact that stigmatism can &quot;upgrade&quot; a latents Demon blood and an adoption pact can create/activate it in non Demon-blooded humans.<br /> <br /> With that said, I think I'll use mine for the purposes of the game I'm running now. But now that understand it, I want to use the original version next time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/demon-the-descent-prestige-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://img513.imageshack.us/img513/4478/8vno.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><br /> Frequent Story Teller for the Circle of Five gaming group.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/654-xiongrey","name":"xiongrey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar654_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"549"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-09-14T13:58:35-07:00","id":256813,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>xiongrey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/174324-heirs-to-hell-questions?p=256760#post256760\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually that clears up all the confusion I had! I was thinking about it too literally in the with the genes tables.<br /> <br /> It makes sense now that demons &quot;activate&quot; or &quot;upgrade&quot; the demon blood within a child. It also makes sense because it's consistent with the fact that stigmatism can &quot;upgrade&quot; a latents Demon blood and an adoption pact can create/activate it in non Demon-blooded humans.<br /> <br /> With that said, I think I'll use mine for the purposes of the game I'm running now. But now that understand it, I want to use the original version next time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Glad to help. :-)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"http://rpg.drivethrustuff.com/browse.php?x=0&amp;y=0&amp;author=Eric%20Zawadzki\" target=